  "english": "[April]\n7. Friday. Tone 1 [ahz]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n23. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahch]. Easter. Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See in order in the first volume.\n\n[June]\n1. Thursday. Tone 8 [dk]. Ascension of Christ.\n11. Sunday. Tone 2 [ak]. Coming of the Holy Spirit.\nPre-fast of the Eliakan [Elijah] Fast.\n18. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahz]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [adz]: \"Who came for salvation.\"\n\n[July]\n9. Sunday. Tone 6 [gk]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [ak]: \"Who came for salvation for the sake of the nation.\"\n23. Sunday. Tone 4 [bk]. Sixth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [bz]: \"Who descended from heaven.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: \"To Thy resurrection.\" Pre-fast of the Vardavar [Transfiguration] Fast.\n30. Sunday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The eating period is one week. Until Saturday, look in the first volume.\n\nAugust\n5. Saturday. Tone 1 [adz]. Of the holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\n6. Sunday. Tone 2 [ak]. Second [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Who of the heavenly hosts.\" Pre-fast of the Holy Mother of God Fast.\n7. Monday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Canticle [Harts] of Fast, Tone 2 [ak]: \"Glorified forever.\"\n13. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahch]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The eating period is four weeks. See in the first volume, verifying the order of this place.\n23. Wednesday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Canticle [Harts] of Fast, Tone 3 [bz]: \"Who is awesome.\"\n26. Saturday. Tone 6 [gk]. Of Thomas the Apostle.\n28. Monday. Tone 8 [dk]. Of Stephen of Ulnia, of Goharines, and others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Holy [God], we bless Thee, Lord.\"\n\nSeptember\n2. Saturday. Tone 5 [gz]. Of James and Simeon the Apostles. Read the scripture and the Gospel of the Tuesday of the Fast of Saint James.\n3. Sunday. Tone 6 [gk]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [bz]: \"We glorify Thee.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk]: \"By the divine grave.\"\n4. Monday. Tone 7 [dz]. Of Andrew the General and his army, etc.\n5. Tuesday. Tone 8 [dk]. Of Adrian and his wife, etc. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Who in the battle of the lawless.\"\n7. Thursday. Tone 2 [ak]. Of Abraham and Khoren, of Cosmas and Damian, and of Astuatsatur the Martyr. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [dz]: \"Who [passed through] the torments.\"\n8. Friday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\n9. Saturday. Tone 4 [bk]. Of the holy Council of Nicaea of the three hundred and eighteen Patriarchs.\n10. Sunday. Tone 5 [gz]. Fifth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Ineffable.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [gz]: \"The oil-bearing [women]\" and \"Today the resurrection.\" Pre-fast of the Holy Cross.\n11. Monday. Tone 6 [gk]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"God of our fathers.\"\n17. Sunday. Tone 4 [bk]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. See in the first volume until the tenth Sunday. But for the Canticles [Harts] of Martyrs and Fasts, the Evening Hymns [Hambartsi] of the Resurrection, and the daily tones, see the second volume, verifying the month.\n\nNovember\n19. Sunday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Tenth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [bz]: \"The voice of good tidings.\" Pre-fast of the Advent [Yisnak] Fast.\n20. Monday. Tone 4 [bk]. Fast of Advent [Yisnak]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [dz]: \"God of our fathers, who delivered.\"\n21. Tuesday. Tone 5 [gz]. Of the Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n25. Saturday. Tone 1 [ahz]. Of Gregory and Nicholas the wonderworking Patriarchs, and of the other Nicholas the Patriarch.",
